----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

let a = 1000

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

let c = a /! b

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

let a_moved = a
set b = b * 2

----------
scriptunit-fragment 5
----------

let d = b + 1

----------
expect all five units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `a` moved |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 250 |
| 3 | reads `a` (1), reads `b` (2) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 8 |
| 4 | takes `a` (1), updates `b` (2) | compiles, runs | new | `a_moved` = 1000 |
| 5 | reads `b` (2) | compiles, runs | new | `d` = 251 |

----------
scriptunit-delete 4
----------

----------
expect unit 4 is deleted
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 4 took `a` when it last ran, and is deleted | `a` = 1000 |
| 2 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 4 updated `b` when it last ran, and is deleted | `b` = 125 |
| 3 | reads `a` (1), reads `b` (2) | untouched | units 1 and 2 provided the same `a` and `b` | `c` = 8 |
| 4 | takes `a` (1), updates `b` (2) | deleted | deleted | - |
| 5 | reads `b` (2) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 4, which no longer updates it | `d` = 126 |

----------
engine
----------

| unit | this step | note |
|------|-----------|------|
| 3 | reruns | a splice reruns every unit from the rerun point on, readers included |
| 5 | recompiles, runs | a removal renumbers every later unit, so they are typechecked under new keys |
